  "body": "## What changed\n\n- `contour_start::exit_at` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_start.rs`) now projects the exit pick onto the fitted walk `walk` instead of the raw polyline `poly`.\n- `nearest_on_walk` and `arc_foot` find the closest point across both `Seg::Line` and `Seg::Arc` moves, snapping within `1e-5` mm (`SNAP_EPS`) of endpoints to prevent sub-lattice slivers.\n- `extend_walk` appends the walk's own lines and arcs along the overlap so rounded corners and fillets re-cut the same moves as the first lap.\n- When an exit pick lands strictly inside a segment, `extend_walk` splits that segment on the first lap as well so both laps emit identical CL moves and the lead-out shares an exact vertex.\n- Added the decision record in `docs/decisions/2195-contour-exit-arcs.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nThe first lap of a closed 2D contour runs through `fit_arcs_sided` (and `fillet_corners` when enabled), which turns rounded corners into `Seg::Arc` moves. `exit_at` previously projected onto and extended from the raw polyline `poly` (`Seg::Line`), emitting straight chords that lie inside and out of phase with the verifier's `arc_chords` tessellation. `verify::crossing` convicted those chords against the first lap's arc and blocked posting.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinning tests in `crates/motion/tests/contour_start.rs`:\n- `an_exit_past_a_rounded_corner_retraces_the_corner_arc_with_no_crossing`\n- `an_exit_inside_a_rounded_corner_arc_splits_both_laps_with_no_crossing`\n- `an_exit_on_an_oblique_wall_and_across_a_blended_corner_has_no_crossing`\n\nMutation checks:\n- Restored `upstream/main` `contour_start.rs`: all three new pinning tests failed with XY feed crossings (including `[5, 15]` and `[5, 17]` on the #2195 fixture).\n- Disabled only the first-lap interior split in `extend_walk`: `an_exit_inside_a_rounded_corner_arc_splits_both_laps_with_no_crossing` failed with XY crossings.\n- Restored the fix: all 14 tests in `contour_start` passed.\n\nGate and lint on the final code:\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: green (`camcraft-motion --lib` and `--test contour_start`, 0 failed).\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-motion --all-targets -- -D warnings`: green with zero warnings.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone (`git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\"` is empty).\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- Did not run `camcraft-app` / MCP / `post` end-to-end tests or the GUI (only `camcraft-motion` changed).\n- Did not run `batch` or `release` gate tiers.\n\n## Overlaps\n\n- PR #1822: touches `crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_start.rs` (`pick_ring`) and `crates/motion/tests/contour_start.rs` (tab tests) — touches the same file, different function; whichever merges second refreshes.\n\nChangelog: Closed 2D contours with an exit point now re-trace fitted arcs and split interior hits cleanly so verify and post accept overlaps around rounded corners (#2195)\n\nEffort: high\n\nFixes #2195\n",
